# Example B1 with a kaon+ beam and everything QBBC gives a kaon that this port does not have,
# switched off. The P1 stage; see muon_emonly.mac beside it for why each line is here.
#
# `ref/oracle/species_processes.csv` for kaon+ is the pion's list with kaon+Inelastic in place of
# pi+Inelastic. Same six inactivations, same reasons.
#
# 200 MeV kaon+: 411.1 mm of water (ref/oracle/hadron_tables.csv, G4_WATER at 199.5262 MeV), so
# it CROSSES B1's 300 mm envelope. Its proper lifetime is 12.38 ns; it enters at beta 0.702 and
# leaves at about 112 MeV and beta 0.58, so mean gamma is about 1.32 and the 330 mm to the world
# boundary takes 1.72 ns against a lab lifetime of 16.3 ns: 1 - exp(-1.72/16.3) = 10% decay in
# flight, and none of them stops. CORRECTED: this read "about 14 cm of water ... it is
# the stopped kaon that decays and this port leaves it stopped", which is wrong by a factor of
# three and wrong about the fate. See muon_emonly.mac for why the distinction matters.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 0

/process/inactivate hadElastic
/process/inactivate kaon+Inelastic
/process/inactivate Decay
/process/inactivate hBrems
/process/inactivate hPairProd
/process/inactivate CoulombScat

/gun/particle kaon+
/gun/energy 200 MeV

/run/printProgress 2000
/run/beamOn 10000
